From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregor MacLennan <gmaclennan@awana.digital>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:20:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: remove upstream-only workflows and config
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream workflows must never run in this repository: a ref containing
the materialized tree (a release tag, or a branch cut from one) would
otherwise carry live push/pull_request-triggered CI. Remove them ALL —
even the schedule/dispatch-only ones that are inert outside upstream's
default branch — because an inert file's triggers can change on any
upstream bump, and a filename allowlist would accept the file while it
went live. With zero workflow files the invariant is trivially
checkable, and verify-patches enforces it: a materialized tree
containing any workflow file fails CI, so an upstream bump that adds
one forces extending this patch. Upstream support files that point at
nodejs/node processes (SUPPORT.md, the issue-template config, the
label-pr config) go too; non-triggering config such as dependabot.yml
is read only from the default branch and is left untouched.
